ct load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A coated article, e.g., a plastic spectacle lens, which has a hard coating film or primer layer having high durability and in which the film is prevented from cracking, peeling, or decreasing in hardness.  This coated article comprises a base and formed on the surface thereof a coating layer comprising titanium oxide and an organic compound of cobalt (II).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un article enrobé, par exemple un verre de lunettes en plastique, revêtu d'une pellicule protectrice ou d'une couche de primaire qui présente une forte durabilité, et qui résiste aux fendillements et aux écaillures tout en gardant sa durabilité. Cet article enrobé comprend une base et, sur sa surface, une couche de revêtement faite d'oxyde de titane et d'un composé organique de cobalt (II).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>